hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","[AI-translation] Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes His heavens and earth in His hands, and says: ""I am Allah"" - and He clenches His fingers and opens them - ""I am the King."" [And the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, swayed to his right and to his left] until I looked at the pulpit moving from its lowest part, until I indeed said: ""Is it falling with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him?"
"2","[AI-translation] The Right Hand of Allah is full; no spending diminishes it, flowing night and day. Have you seen what He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? It has not diminished what is in His Right Hand. He said: And His Throne is upon water, and in His other Hand is the grasping; He raises and lowers."
"3","[AI-translation] Say: ""What Allah willed, then you willed,"" and say: ""By the Lord of the Ka'bah."
"4","[AI-translation] Whoever swears, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah."
"5","[AI-translation] Tufayl saw a dream and informed whoever he informed among you. You used to say a word that modesty prevented me from forbidding to you. He said: Do not say: ""What Allah willed and what Muhammad willed."
"6","[AI-translation] Have you made me an equal to Allah? (In another wording: a partner?!). No, rather what Allah alone willed."
"7","[AI-translation] When one of you swears, let him not say: ""What Allah willed and you willed,"" but let him say: ""What Allah willed, then you willed."
"8","[AI-translation] If you knew the extent of the mercy of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, you would rely upon it and do no deeds, and if you knew the extent of His anger, nothing would benefit you."
"9","[AI-translation] Reflect upon the bounties of Allah, but do not reflect upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"10","[AI-translation] I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant testifies to them truthfully except that Allah protects him from the heat of the Fire."
"11","[AI-translation] And I bear witness, and bear witness: that no one bears witness to it except that he is free from polytheism. He means the two testimonies of faith."
"12","[AI-translation] There is no soul that dies while it bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, with that returning to a certain heart, except that Allah forgives it."
"13","[AI-translation] Five things none knows them except Allah: * (Indeed, with Allah is the knowledge of the Hour. He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. And no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware)"
"14","[AI-translation] Receive glad tidings, receive glad tidings! Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. He said: Then this Quran is a rope, one end of which is in the hand of Allah and the other end is in your hands. So hold fast to it, for you will never go astray and never be destroyed after it ever."
"15","[AI-translation] Allah, Blessed and Exalted be He, said: The good deed is by ten times its like or more, and the evil deed is by one or I forgive it. Even if you were to meet Me with an earthful of sins, as long as you do not associate partners with Me, I would meet you with an earthful of forgiveness."
"16","[AI-translation] Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Whoever does a good deed, for him is ten times its like or more; and whoever does an evil deed, its reward is the like of it or I forgive. Whoever does an earthful of sin, then meets Me not associating anything with Me, I make for him the like of it in forgiveness. And whoever comes to Me a span, I come to him a cubit; and whoever comes to Me a cubit, I come to him an arm's length; and whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him running."
"17","[AI-translation] Whoever meets Allah not associating anything with Him, and has not been stained with unlawful blood, enters Paradise."
"18","[AI-translation] Whoever declares the oneness of Allah, Exalted be He, and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and blood are inviolable, and his reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"19","[AI-translation] That was Jibril who appeared to me at the side of the Harrah and said: Give glad tidings to your Ummah that whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise. I said: O Jibril, even if he stole and committed fornication? He said: Yes. He said: I said: Even if he stole and committed fornication? He said: Yes. He said: I said: Even if he stole and committed fornication? He said: Yes, even if he drank wine."
"20","There was a man among those who came before you who had never done any good deed whatsoever except for the declaration of monotheism (Tawheed). When death approached him, he said to his family: ""Look, when I die, burn me until I become ashes, then grind me, then scatter me on a windy day; [then scatter half of me on land and half in the sea. By Allah, if Allah has power over me, He will punish me with a punishment the like of which He has not inflicted on anyone in the worlds]."" When he died, they did that to him. [Then Allah commanded the land to gather what was in it, and commanded the sea to gather what was in it], and there he was, [standing] in the Hand of Allah. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: ""O son of Adam! What drove you to do what you did?"" He said: ""My Lord, fear of You (and in another narration: awe of You, and You know best)."" He said: ""So He forgave him because of that, and he had never done any good deed whatsoever except the declaration of monotheism."""
"21","[AI-translation] As for your father, had he affirmed the Oneness, your fasting and giving charity on his behalf would have benefited him."
"22","[AI-translation] No, he used to give for the sake of this world, its mention, and its praise, and he never said: 'My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment.'"
"23","[AI-translation] I call to Allah alone, the One whom if harm touches you and you call upon Him, He removes it from you; and the One whom if you become lost in a barren land and you call upon Him, He returns you; and the One whom if drought strikes you and you call upon Him, He causes vegetation to grow for you."
"24","[AI-translation] Allah Almighty said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"25","[AI-translation] Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created you? He says: Allah. He says: Then who created Allah?! If any of you finds this, let him read: I believe in Allah and His messengers, for that will remove it from him."
"26","[AI-translation] People will not cease asking, saying: What is such and such? Until they say: Allah is the creator of people, so who created Allah? At that point, they go astray."
"27","[AI-translation] Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created such and such? Who created such and such? Who created such and such? Until he says: Who created your Lord?! When he reaches that, let him seek refuge in Allah and stop."
"28","[AI-translation] People will soon be questioning one another until one of them says: Allah created creation, so who created Allah Almighty? If they say that, then say: ""Allah is One, Allah is the Eternal Refuge, He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent."" Then let one of you spit to his left three times, and seek refuge from Satan."
"29","[AI-translation] Go out and call among the people: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, Paradise is guaranteed for him."
"30","[AI-translation] Receive glad tidings, and give glad tidings to those behind you, that whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah truthfully will enter Paradise."
"31","[AI-translation] Whoever says: There is no god but Allah (sincerely) will enter Paradise."
"32","[AI-translation] Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise."
"33","[AI-translation] Go with these two sandals; whoever you meet behind this wall who bears witness that there is no god but Allah with his heart being certain of it, give him the glad tidings of Paradise."
"34","[AI-translation] Ghatfani."
"35","[AI-translation] I command you with four, and forbid you from four: Belief in Allah. Then he explained it to them, saying: Testifying that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah - and he clenched one - establishing the prayer, giving zakat, and that you give one-fifth of what you gain as spoils. And I forbid you from Dubba', Hantam, Naqir, and Muqayyar."
"36","[AI-translation] Increase in saying the testimony that there is no god but Allah before a barrier is set between you and it, and prompt your dying with it."
"37","[AI-translation] Whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire."
"38","Come, pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill your children, nor bring forth a slander you fabricate between your hands and feet, nor disobey me in what is right. Whoever among you fulfills this, his reward is with Allah. Whoever commits any of these and is punished for it in this world, that will be an expiation for him. Whoever commits any of these and Allah conceals it, his matter is with Allah: if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him."
"39","[AI-translation] That was Jibril who appeared to me at the side of the Harrah and said: Give glad tidings to your Ummah that whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise. I said: O Jibril, even if he stole and committed zina? He said: Yes. He said: I said: Even if he stole and committed zina? He said: Yes. He said: I said: Even if he stole and committed zina? He said: Yes, even if he drank wine."
"40","[AI-translation] Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam."
"41","[AI-translation] As for your father, had he affirmed Tawhid, and you fasted and gave charity on his behalf, it would have benefited him."
"42","[AI-translation] Indeed, my father and your father are in the Fire."
"43","[AI-translation] No, O 'Aisha, he never used to say: ""My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment."
"44","[AI-translation] When a servant embraces Islam and does well in his Islam, Allah records for him every good deed he ever did, and erases from him every bad deed he ever did. Then thereafter is the reckoning: a good deed is multiplied ten times to seven hundred times, and a bad deed is by its like, unless Allah Almighty overlooks it."
"45","[AI-translation] No, he used to give for the sake of the world, its mention, and its praise, and he never once said: ""My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment."
"46","[AI-translation] I have embraced Islam upon the good I have sent forth."
"47","[AI-translation] When a servant embraces Islam and does well in his Islam, Allah records for him every good deed he ever did, and erases from him every bad deed he ever did. Then thereafter is the reckoning: a good deed is multiplied ten times to seven hundred times, and a bad deed is by its like, unless Allah Almighty overlooks it."
"48","[AI-translation] I have embraced Islam upon the good I have sent forth."
"49","[AI-translation] Whoever does well in what remains, it is forgiven for him what has passed; and whoever does evil in what remains, he is held accountable for what has passed and what remains."
"50","[AI-translation] Islamic period; and whoever does evil in Islam is taken to account for the first and the last."
"51","[AI-translation] Whoever from the People of the Book embraces Islam, he has his reward twice, and he has the likes of what we have, and upon him is the likes of what is upon us; and whoever from the polytheists embraces Islam, he has his reward, and he has the likes of what we have, and upon him is the likes of what is upon us."
